QuestGuidance.Register("en",9,{
[257]="70046BFD\n1\tSpook Mordor searchers (total: 6)\030Spook Khundolar searchers (total: 6)\tOrcs and Khundolar searchers can be found throughout central and north-central North Ithilien. Rhadrog has asked you to scare the forces of Mordor that are searching North Ithilien for the Rangers. You should roar at the searchers while you remain hidden from their sight.\n2\tTalk to Rhadrog\tRhadrog can be found at Henneth Annûn in north-central North Ithilien. You have unnerved many of the Enemy's forces in North Ithilien and should now return to Rhadrog.\n",
[258]="70043098\n1\tAngbor's men can be found throughout the eastern half of Pelargir. Angbor has asked you to rally his men in Pelargir before he sets out into Upper Lebennin.\t\n2\tTalk to Angbor in Pelargir\tAngbor can be found by the eastern gate of Pelargir. You have rallied many of Angbor's men and should now return to Angbor.\n",
[259]="70030B96\n1\tCollect meat from the most dangerous beasts in the Sutcrofts (total: 6)\tRook wants you to hunt the most dangerous beasts in the Sutcrofts. He mentioned that they are nearby, but will not say more.\n2\tTalk to Rook\tRook can be found to the west of Snowbourn.\n",
[260]="700193C4\n1\tDefeat hendrevail in the Vale of Thráin (total: 12)\tThe road runs northwards from Noglond through the Vale of Thráin to Thorin's Halls. Ketill has asked you to patrol along the road through the Vale of Thráin and cull the numbers of hendrevail. He also mentioned that hendrevail could be found in large numbers south of the river to the south of Noglond.\n2\tTalk to Ketill at Noglond\tKetill is in Noglond, south of Thorin's Hall. You should return to Ketill and report the results of your patrol.\n",
[261]="7003E2FA\n1\tInvestigate the strange tomb\tThe strange tomb can be found north-west of Mincham's Camp, in the Fields of Fornost. You should investigate the strange tomb.\n2\tInvestigate the strange tomb\tThe strange tomb can be found north-west of Mincham's Camp, in the Fields of Fornost. You should investigate the strange tomb.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have dispersed Morrafn's fell light from this haunted place.\n",
[262]="70017524\n1\tDefeat glow-worms in the Dark Delving (total: 50)\tThe Dark Delvings lie far to the south-east of the Shadowed Refuge. Ymar's nightmares continue, and he needs you to help him rid them from his mind. He asked you to breach the Dark Delvings and kill the glow-worms there to set his mind at ease.\n2\tReturn to Ymar at the Shadowed Refuge\tYmar is at the Shadowed Refuge, far to the north-west of the Dark Delvings. You found the glow-worms within the Dark Delvings and defeated them as Ymar had asked.\n",
[263]="7001758C\n1\tDefeat Cracktooth in Skûmfil\tCracktooth is in Skûmfil in Moria, east of the Shadowed Refuge in the Foundations of Stone. You should defeat and search the deep-claw named Cracktooth in Skûmfil, for it is likely that the last bit of text can be found upon that beast.\n2\tReturn to Pada at the Foundations of Stone\tPada awaits your return at the Foundations of Stone in Moria. You have defeated Cracktooth and recovered the lost text missing from the composition being compiled. The completed work should help you on your way to being a truly heroic Minstrel.\n",
[264]="70016B41\n1\tSeek information about the axe\030Talk to Kafli at the Orc-watch\tThere are dwarves encamped in the Twenty-first Hall. You found an axe in the remains of Balin's expedition's camp. It is drawing the attention of every dwarf you meet. Perhaps you should ask someone about it.\n2\tSpeak to Kafli at the Orc-watch\tKafli may be found at the Orc-watch, far to the south of here. You were told to speak with a dwarf named Kafli about the axe.\n",
[265]="70016B42\n1\tSeek information about the axe\tThere are dwarves in the Twenty-first Hall. You should, perhaps, speak with someone regarding the axe you found.\n2\tSpeak to Kafli at the Orc-watch\tKafli may be found at the Orc-watch, far to the south of the Twenty-first Hall. You were told to speak with a dwarf named Kafli about the axe you found.\n",
[266]="7000D75D\n1\tCollect the bouquet from the vase at the wrong door\tThe bouquet is in a vase near the wrong door on the Scholar's Stair in Bree. Avery Crabapple has asked you to collect the bouquet from the wrong address.\n2\tTalk to Fern Coppersmith\030Ask a neighbour about the address\tThe neighbours are upon the Scholar's Stair in Bree. Avery Crabapple asked you to inquire of the neighbours for her address.\n3\tCollect the sweets\tFern Coppersmith's sweets are in the alley behind Avery Crabapple. Fern Coppersmith asked you to collect her sweets from the wrong door.\n4\tGive the sweets to Crabapple\tAvery Crabapple is in the Bree Market. You should bring the sweets to Avery Crabapple.\n",
[267]="700479E7\n1\tComplete 'In the Spirit of Yule' five more times\tEvery day there is something to do in Frostbluff. Every day there is Yule! Come and join everyone in Frostbluff and participate in many Yule Festival activities for five more days!\n2\tComplete 'In the Spirit of Yule' (total: 5)\tEvery day there is something to do in Frostbluff. Every day there is Yule! Come and join everyone in Frostbluff and participate in many Yule Festival activities for five more days!\n3\tTalk to Mara Sandydowns\tMara Sandydowns would like to thank you for your continued participation in the Yule Festival.\n",
[268]="7004C98E\n1\tComplete 'In the Spirit of Yule' three more times\tEvery day there is something to do in Frostbluff. Every day there is Yule! Come and join everyone in Frostbluff and participate in many Yule Festival activities for three more days!\n2\tComplete 'In the Spirit of Yule' (total: 3)\tEvery day there is something to do in Frostbluff. Every day there is Yule! Come and join everyone in Frostbluff and participate in many Yule Festival activities for three more days!\n3\tTalk to Mara Sandydowns\tMara Sandydowns would like to thank you for your continued participation in the Yule Festival.\n",
[269]="700479E6\n1\tComplete 'In the Spirit of Yule' five more times\tEvery day there is something to do in Frostbluff. Every day there is Yule! Come and join everyone in Frostbluff and participate in many Yule Festival activities for five more days!\n2\tComplete 'In the Spirit of Yule' (total: 5)\tEvery day there is something to do in Frostbluff. Every day there is Yule! Come and join everyone in Frostbluff and participate in many Yule Festival activities for five more days!\n3\tTalk to Mara Sandydowns\tMara Sandydowns would like to thank you for your continued participation in the Yule Festival.\n",
[270]="7004C991\n1\tComplete 'In the Spirit of Yule' three more times\tEvery day there is something to do in Frostbluff. Every day there is Yule! Come and join everyone in Frostbluff and participate in many Yule Festival activities for three more days!\n2\tComplete 'In the Spirit of Yule' (total: 3)\tEvery day there is something to do in Frostbluff. Every day there is Yule! Come and join everyone in Frostbluff and participate in many Yule Festival activities for three more days!\n3\tTalk to Mara Sandydowns\tMara Sandydowns would like to thank you for your continued participation in the Yule Festival.\n",
[271]="700479E5\n1\tComplete 'In the Spirit of Yule' five more times\tEvery day there is something to do in Frostbluff. Every day there is Yule! Come and join everyone in Frostbluff and participate in many Yule Festival activities for five more days!\n2\tComplete 'In the Spirit of Yule' (total: 5)\tEvery day there is something to do in Frostbluff. Every day there is Yule! Come and join everyone in Frostbluff and participate in many Yule Festival activities for five more days!\n3\tTalk to Mara Sandydowns\tMara Sandydowns would like to thank you for your continued participation in the Yule Festival.\n",
[272]="7004C98F\n1\tComplete 'In the Spirit of Yule' three more times\tEvery day there is something to do in Frostbluff. Every day there is Yule! Come and join everyone in Frostbluff and participate in many Yule Festival activities for three more days!\n2\tComplete 'In the Spirit of Yule' (total: 3)\tEvery day there is something to do in Frostbluff. Every day there is Yule! Come and join everyone in Frostbluff and participate in many Yule Festival activities for three more days!\n3\tTalk to Mara Sandydowns\tMara Sandydowns would like to thank you for your continued participation in the Yule Festival.\n",
[273]="700479E4\n1\tComplete 'In the Spirit of Yule' five times\tEvery day there is something to do in Frostbluff. Every day there is Yule! Come and join everyone in Frostbluff and participate in many Yule Festival activities for five days!\n2\tComplete 'In the Spirit of Yule' (total: 5)\tEvery day there is something to do in Frostbluff. Every day there is Yule! Come and join everyone in Frostbluff and participate in many Yule Festival activities for five days!\n3\tTalk to Mara Sandydowns\tMara Sandydowns would like to thank you for your continued participation in the Yule Festival.\n",
[274]="7004C992\n1\tComplete 'In the Spirit of Yule' three times\tEvery day there is something to do in Frostbluff. Every day there is Yule! Come and join everyone in Frostbluff and participate in many Yule Festival activities for three days!\n2\tComplete 'In the Spirit of Yule' (total: 3)\tEvery day there is something to do in Frostbluff. Every day there is Yule! Come and join everyone in Frostbluff and participate in many Yule Festival activities for three days!\n3\tTalk to Mara Sandydowns\tMara Sandydowns would like to thank you for your continued participation in the Yule Festival.\n",
[275]="7004A389\n1\tCheck this stage in the quest journal.\t\n2\tAccept surrenders (total: 10)\tAccept the surrender of any Forgeworkers or Men who offer it.\n3\tVisit the Udûn Foothold\tYou should visit the Udûn Foothold to check on the fate of the surrendered peoples.\n",
[276]="700032D7\n1\tBring the journal leaves to Wilimar Bolger\030Collect journal leaves (total: 3)\tWolves can be found east of Budgeford. Without the missing leaves, it will be impossible to determine who shot the arrow in Wilimar Bolger's door, nor why. Wilimar suspects that wolves tore the journal apart and has asked you to try to recover the leaves from them.\n",
[277]="700455DC\n1\tDefeat foes on the Pelennor Fields (total: 30)\tFoes can be found across the Pelennor Fields. Burnoth has asked you to aid in the Battle of the Pelennor Fields by defeating many of the Enemy's forces.\n2\tBattle your way to the centre of the Pelennor Fields\tEnemies are on all sides! Hold the field and protect those you can! You have defeated many of the Enemy's forces and should now continue to aid the forces of Gondor and Rohan on the field. Note: You must complete Book 6, Chapter 2 of Volume IV to advance this objective.\n3\tSearch for the Riders Three at Kings' End\tKings' End can be found near the centre of the Pelennor Fields at the site where Théoden King fell. You have arrived at Kings' End and should now seek out the Riders Three.\n4\tTalk to Ulf at Kings' End\030Talk to Hutha at Kings' End\tBurnoth, Hutha, and Ulf can be found at Kings' End. You have found the Riders Three at Kings' End and should now speak to them.\n5\tPlant Léofdag's spear, Wrecend, in the ground at Kings' End\tA small mound of earth can be found near the site where Théoden King fell at Kings' End. Hutha has asked you to plant Léofdag's spear near the site where Théoden King fell.\n6\tTalk to Burnoth at Kings' End\tBurnoth can be found at Kings' End. You have honoured Léofdag's memory by laying his spear at the site where his King fell. You should now speak to Burnoth.\n",
[278]="7004A81C\n1\tDefeat foes in Dâr Mauzur (total: 12)\030Destroy Orkish barriers in Dâr Mauzur (total: 8)\tBregdal has asked you to defeat foes in Dâr Mauzur and destroy Orkish barriers.\n",
[279]="700250F3\n1\tGo to Mara Sandydowns, for she wishes to speak with you\tMara Sandydowns can be found near the entrance to Winter-home. You should speak with Mara Sandydowns, for everyone says she is looking for you.\n2\tTalk to Mara Sandydowns when you are ready to hear the choice she will ask you to make.\tMara Sandydowns can be found near the entrance to Winter-home. You should speak with Mara Sandydowns, for she is about to present you with an important decision.\n3\tMara Sandydowns can be found near the entrance to Winter-home. She is presenting you with a choice, either help the poor or help the rich of Winter-home.\t\n4\tMara Sandydowns can be found near the entrance to Winter-home. Return and speak to Mara Sandydowns now that you have cast your lot one way or the other.\t\n",
[280]="7007161D\n1\tRescue imprisoned thralls (total: 6)\030Defeat Ordâkhai inside Esh Mêkag prison (total: 15)\030Defeat Warden Khusóku\tA new warden has taken control of Esh Mêkag and is threatening to execute the thralls remaining inside. You should rescue the imprisoned thralls, and defeat the Ordâkhai inside Esh Mêkag prison.\n2\tTalk to Ebuzâm\tThe remaining thralls have been rescued and the new warden defeated. You should return to Ebuzâm.\n",
[281]="70047BD1\n1\tBurn the remains of the slain at Ondoher's Folly (total: 10)\tDefiled remains can be found throughout Ondoher's Folly, in north-western Dagorlad. You have discovered the grim remains of many slain prisoners and slaves at Ondoher's Folly. You should burn them before the Orcs can defile them further.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have burned many of the slain at Ondoher's Folly and prevented the Orcs from further defiling their remains.\n",
[282]="70017509\n1\tDefeat the Watcher in the Water\tThe Watcher in the Water lairs within the Vile Maw. Kaldi warned you that the foe within the Vile Maw was one that would drag the very hearts of those near it towards oblivion without the great power of light on their side. Be cautious and take two fellowships of your staunchest allies.\n2\tTalk to Kaldi outside of the Vile Maw\tKaldi is at the encampment outside of the Vile Maw. Your victory over the Watcher in the Water will be held as a great triumph amongst the dwarves.\n",
[283]="7004956D\n1\tDeliver Gimli's message to the Firehorns at the hidden gate of the Oath-taker's Horn\tThe hidden gate of Lûghash can be found in an alcove high above the main gate, accessible by a rear pathway leading onto the Spire. Gimli has asked you to deliver a message to the Firehorns in the Oath-taker's Horn. He hopes that King Greytooth might be convinced to treat upon the plains of Dor Amarth.\n2\tDeliver Gimli's message to the Firehorns at the main gate of the Oath-taker's Horn\tThe main gate of the Oath-taker's Horn can be found in the vale far below the hidden gate. You have tried to enter the hidden gate and have found that the Firehorns have begun to seal it from within. You should now try the main gate.\n3\tCall forth the Firehorns and deliver Gimli's message\tThe gate mechanism can be found beside the main gate of the Oath-taker's Horn. You have arrived at the main gate of the Oath-taker's Horn. You should use the gate mechanism and call forth the Firehorns to deliver Gimli's message.\n4\tTalk to Gimli outside the Oath-taker's Horn\tGimli can be found along the causeway outside the Oath-taker's Horn. You were brutally attacked by the Firehorns, and they threatened the Dwarves of Durin's Folk. You should talk to Gimli and tell him what has happened.\n",
[284]="7005A802\n1\tTalk to King Thráin\tKing Thráin can be found outside Muru Azog at Azanulbizar. After the defeat of Azog and the clearing of Orkish filth from Azanulbizar, King Thráin wishes to honour his father, Thrór. You should talk to King Thráin.\n2\tTalk to King Thráin at Amdân\tKing Thráin can be found at Amdân. After the burning of the dead at Azanulbizar, King Thráin and the survivors of the Sixth War of the Dwarves and Orcs have returned to Amdân. You should talk to King Thráin.\n3\tTalk to Dáin Ironfoot\tDáin can be found at Amdân. After the burning of the dead at Azanulbizar, King Thráin and the survivors of the Sixth War of the Dwarves and Orcs have returned to Amdân. You should talk to Dáin.\n",
[285]="7000D7FD\n1\tCollect as many flowers as you can in one hour\tPatches of violets can be found in Bree-land. Patches of primroses can be found in Ered Luin. Patches of marigolds can be found in the Shire. Gredlan Mugwort is in Bree-town. Avery Crabapple has asked you to collect flowers from throughout Bree-land, Ered Luin, and the Shire and bring them to Gredlan Mugwort.\n",
[286]="70000050\n1\tBring lynx-meat to Old Mugwort\030Collect lynx-meat (total: 8)\tLynx can be found throughout Nain Enidh -- the central Lone-lands -- north and north-east of the encampment at the east edge of Minas Eriol. Old Mugwort believes he has come up with a way to drive goblins and Wargs from the Lone-lands, but he needs you to collect lynx-meat first.\n",
[287]="700381C5\n1\tAid Gimli and his allies in completing their patrol ([see journal]/4)\tAid Gimli in removing enemy threats that have managed to flank the defenders on the wall, while others work to rescue supplies from besieged structures within the deep. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[288]="7005AB02\n1\tDefeat Héormuth\tNáth has told you about a huge white sabre-cat lurking somewhere near Fellgát. You should find and defeat the sabre-cat known as Héormuth.\n2\tTalk to Náth in Fellgát\tYou have successfully defeated the sabre-cat menacing the dwarves in Fellgát. You should talk to Náth.\n",
})
